.TH brother-td-filter 7 "2026-11-17" "brother-td-cups 1.0.0" "Driver Manual"
.SH NAME
brother-td-filter \- CUPS raster filter for Brother TD-4D label printers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/lib/cups/filter/brother-td-filter
.I job-id user title copies options
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brother-td-filter
is a CUPS filter.
It reads a CUPS raster stream
.RB ( application/vnd.cups-raster )
from standard input, converts each page to one-bit monochrome, and writes
Brother TD-4D raster commands to standard output.
The output is sent to the printer by the CUPS backend configured for the
queue.
.PP
The filter is normally started by
.BR cupsd (8)
and should not be run by hand except for diagnostics.
.SH OPTIONS
All driver options are passed in the
.I options
argument by CUPS. They correspond to the PPD options described in
.BR brother-td (7).
The most important options are:
.TP
.B TDModel
The printer model. It selects the head width and the invalidate sequence.
.TP
.B TDMediaType
.B DieCut
or
.BR Continuous .
.TP
.B TDDither
Monochrome conversion algorithm. The default is
.BR Floyd .
.TP
.B TDThreshold
Threshold value from 0 to 255. The default is 128.
.TP
.B TDScaling
.BR Fit ,
.BR FitEnlarge ,
.BR Crop ,
or
.BR None .
.TP
.B TDRotate
Rotation in degrees: 0, 90, 180, or 270.
.TP
.B TDInvert ", " TDMirror ", " TDBorder
Boolean image options.
.TP
.B TDAlignX ", " TDAlignY
Placement of the image inside the printable area.
.TP
.B TDMargin
Feed margin for continuous media in millimetres.
.TP
.B TDAutoTrim
Trim blank rows on continuous media.
.TP
.B TDAutoCut ", " TDCutAtEnd ", " TDPeeler
Finishing options for continuous media.
.TP
.B TDCompression
.B TIFF
(PackBits) or
.BR None .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BROTHER_TD_DEBUG
If set to a non-empty value other than
.B 0
or
.BR false ,
the filter logs detailed geometry and option information to standard error,
which CUPS writes to its error log.
.TP
.B BROTHER_TD_DEBUG_DIR
If set to a writable directory, the filter writes the exact byte stream sent
to the printer to
.IR job-\fIid\fB.prn .
The CUPS filter user (usually
.BR lp )
must be able to create files in the directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The input was invalid, an option was unsupported, memory was exhausted, or a
write error occurred.
.SH NOTES
The filter emits
.B Z
for blank raster rows, uses TIFF/PackBits when beneficial, and sends
.B FF
between pages and
.B Ctrl-Z
after the last page. It finishes with
.B "ESC i a ff"
to return the printer to its default command mode.
.PP
Die-cut labels use a zero feed margin. Continuous media uses the configured
feed margin and can be trimmed automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brother-td (7),
.BR cups (1),
.BR cupsd (8)
